<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady, limited plant demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady, limited plant demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets on Tueasday on limited demand from processing plants, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were around 3,000 tonnes on low volumes.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent rose by 400 rupees per tonne on very limited supply from processing plants against good demand from vanaspati units and refineries. Soyoil refined was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were steady but there was little trade.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was quoted at $270-271 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction prices were down as foreign buyers were offering very low prices.</p>
<p>Dealers said buyers offered $125 while sellers offers were $130 per tonne in export for Indian rapeseed extraction.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was 4,400 rupees per tonne FOR Bedibunder and 4,350 rupees FOR Bhavnagar. Business volume was low and the undertone was weak.</p>
